  "statement": "The points are $A(1,2,3)$, $B(4,0,1)$ and $C(0,1,2)$. Find the angle $ABC$ (to the nearest degree).",
  "solution": "$$\\vec{BA}=(1-4,\\,2-0,\\,3-1)=(-3,2,2),\\qquad \\vec{BC}=(0-4,\\,1-0,\\,2-1)=(-4,1,1).$$\n$$\\vec{BA}\\cdot\\vec{BC}=(-3)(-4)+2(1)+2(1)=12+2+2=16.$$\n$$|\\vec{BA}|=\\sqrt{9+4+4}=\\sqrt{17},\\qquad |\\vec{BC}|=\\sqrt{16+1+1}=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt2.$$\nSo\n$$\\cos\\angle ABC=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot3\\sqrt2}=\\frac{16}{3\\sqrt{34}}\\approx0.9147,$$\nand $\\angle ABC\\approx23.9^{\\circ}$, i.e. about $24^{\\circ}$.",
